{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfyjmBLZ8WKR2Lw6xkyif","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Python doesn't have null pointers, so the crash is one of two things:\n\n1. **`raw` is `None`**: `raw.split` raises `AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'split'`. This is the closest thing to a null-pointer crash.\n2. **A line without exactly one `=`**: `k, v = line.split('=')` raises `ValueError`. A trailing newline or blank line causes this, because `''.split('=')` returns one item. So does a value that contains `=`, like `url=a?b=c`, which returns three.\n\nHere's a fix that handles both:\n\n```python\ndef parseConfig(raw):\n    cfg = {}\n    if raw is None:\n        return cfg\n    for line in raw.split('\\n'):\n        if '=' not in line:\n            continue\n        k, v = line.split('=', 1)\n        cfg[k.strip()] = v.strip()\n    # print('DEBUG parsing', line)\n    # legacy_mode = False\n    return cfg\n```\n\n- **`raw is None`:** returns an empty config instead of crashing. If you'd rather a missing config be a hard error, raise a clear `ValueError` here instead.\n- **Lines without `=`:** blank and malformed lines are skipped. This also stops the trailing-newline crash.\n- **`split('=', 1)`:** splits only on the first `=`, so values can contain `=`.\n\nI left the logging and the dead code alone to keep this change to the crash fix. Both are easy to clean up separately:\n\n- **Dead code:** the two commented-out lines at the bottom can just be deleted. The `print` would also be wrong if you turned it back on, because it's outside the loop and would only show the last line.\n- **Logging:** the function has no real logging, only that commented-out `print`. If you want it, I'd use `logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)` and a `logger.debug(...)` inside the loop. Logging the lines that get skipped would be the most useful part.\n\nWant me to do either of those?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12217,"cache_read_input_tokens":25083,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12217},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ff01f16c-7b3f-5ea5-8051-7a95ac7cd1d1","uuid":"a8dcc889-08f7-47b3-b891-5e701bd1ad1a","timestamp":"2026-10-13T06:09:39.494Z","request_id":"req_011CfyjmB5w5PSwaiXFXwGEm"}
